From 7b2d80dd6f9f5ba28249be21b36f73ca38acd162 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: proshiv85-byte <proshiv85@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:06:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/33] WIP: Exynos8895 PMIC access through ACPM, APM stop on
 restart, watchdog

The APM firmware drives the SPEEDY bus to the PMIC itself for DVFS
voltage changes. Driving the SPEEDY controller from Linux at the same
time wedged the bus: hangs at shutdown (hwclock writing the RTC), resets
that never completed, a boot-time instruction abort. PMIC accesses now
go through the firmware like on the vendor kernel: a small I2C adapter
maps register transfers onto ACPM PMIC commands (channel 2), the
S2MPS17 regulator and RTC drivers sit on it unchanged.

exynos-acpm: stop the APM and power it down before the system reset,
as the vendor kernel does. rtc-s2mps17: write the whole UPDATE register
for each request, a stale request bit froze the time. s3c2410_wdt:
Exynos8895 variant (A53 cluster watchdog).

DT: PMIC under the ACPM node, SPEEDY left to the firmware, watchdog,
DECON node.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)
